# Capture Policy and Failure Containment

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M2 Core utility
Dependencies: 03_CAPTURE_PROOF.todo, 05_WINDOW_SHELL.todo

## Purpose

Apply capture exclusion before sensitive reveal and handle detected failures honestly.

## Tasks

- [ ] Implement per-HWND-generation setup/invalidated/fault states and centralized reveal permission.
- [x] Check Windows11/DWM and set WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE on the owned top-level window.
- [x] Capture native errors immediately; retain getter outcomes as separate local diagnostics.
- [ ] Prevent stale async callbacks from binding/showing notes on a new or unconfigured handle.
- [ ] Implement only spike-proven first-show/composition ordering; no arbitrary protection delay.
- [x] Hide before mode style changes; reapply before every permitted reveal.
- [x] Hide/stop on display/session/lock/power notifications; require deliberate reveal.
- [ ] Audit secondary surfaces; use inline UI or protect/redesign every app-owned note-bearing surface.
- [ ] Show generic actionable error/status without sensitive text or false 'invisible' certification.
- [ ] Inject setter failure, contradictory readback, disposed handle, and capability failure.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] No tested startup/recreation path renders notes before successful setup for its current HWND.
- [ ] Detected failure leaves content hidden, preserves the document, and provides recovery/exit.
- [ ] No silent downgrade to WDA_NONE, WDA_MONITOR, or unprotected secondary window.
- [ ] Getter-unavailable and capture-unverified are distinct from setter failure and observed pixel results.
- [ ] Documentation states unobservable recorder bypasses and past captured frames remain outside control.

## Completion evidence

- Shared native adapter and WPF reveal/fault paths implemented; local synthetic GDI samples pass.
- Full per-generation/failure/first-frame/secondary-surface and remote-product evidence remains open.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-07 - Planned; based on Microsoft API contracts and explicit empirical gates.
